  "text": [
    "A controversial issue regarding intravitreal bevacizumab use centers on whether it increases retinal ischemia  .",
    "Terui et al. showed that changes in the capillary nonperfusion area were insignificant 1 month after intravitreal bevacizumab injection [29] .",
    "This result is compatible with ours, as the areas of capillary nonperfusion were not significantly changed after injection in our study.",
    "Our data also showed that the changes at 3 and 6 months after the injection were not significantly different between the 2 treatment schedules.",
    "Collectively, these data suggest that intravitreal bevacizumab injections do not aggravate retinal ischemia in patients with BRVO."
  ],
